# FoodomicsPy

**FoodomicsPy** is an open-source Python package for foodomics data analysis

## Features

- Read Bruker OPUS and HDF5 datasets
- Spectral preprocessing (SNV, mean centering, autoscaling, Savitzky–Golay)
- NMR spectral alignment
- Partial least-squares (PLS) regression with cross-validation
- Interactive FTIR and NMR visualization
- Publication-ready plotting utilities

## Installation

```bash
pip install foodomicspy
```

Or install the latest development version:

```bash
git clone https://github.com/UmrbekMavlanov/FoodomicsPy.git
cd FoodomicsPy
pip install .
```

## Quick example

```python
import foodomicspy as f

# Read spectra
df = f.io.read_hdf("spectra.h5")

# Preprocess
df = f.preprocessing.snv(df)

# Perform PLS
result = f.chemometrics.perform_pls(
    X=df,
    y=y,
)

# Plot results
f.plotting.plot_pls(result)
```

